>Say I am a lawful Character and I kill a neutral unicorn, the altar
>next to me is also neutral, should I offer it, or should I convert
>the altar to my allignment first.
>
>in other words, I should be co-alligned with the altar I am offering
>the non-co-alligned unicorn on. The unicorn doesn't have to
>be co-alligned with the altar that I am offering it on. correct ?
>                                                       -David

Correct.  #offer non-aligned unicorns on co-aligned altars.
So, if you are lawful, sacrifice black and gray(grey?) unicorns
on a lawful altar.

#offering a unicorn that is co-aligned with the altar you are sacrificing
on is a BAD idea.  This means that your lawful character shouldn't #offer
a black unicorn on a chaotic altar.  (or a gray unicorn on a neutral alter).

